            <ArticleTitle>The role of interleukin-6 in nociception and pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1096-103, table of contents</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">That IL-6 is an interesting target in the study of pain is underscored by its biomolecular properties, its localization after experimental pain, and its modulating effect on pain after administration.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
